[{:db/id 17592186119848 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-27db2f89-f211-5a22-8370-a36f3eeeed25"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119849 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-71b4ed44-551f-59fd-a0cd-dc5bcd55b071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-27db2f89-f211-5a22-8370-a36f3eeeed25" :question/id #uuid "27db2f89-f211-5a22-8370-a36f3eeeed25" :question/math-academy-id "q-139965" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $A$ and $B$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$A$  and $B$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b93d2a3e-8872-5847-9667-8c3c236eb8e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b93d2a3e-8872-5847-9667-8c3c236eb8e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b93d2a3e-8872-5847-9667-8c3c236eb8e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49a263fb-b924-566b-a1a2-e05321e1d5e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49a263fb-b924-566b-a1a2-e05321e1d5e8" "answer-e0dfb5d5-ea82-565b-84e6-679186a0f012" "answer-eb250ee6-15f1-5344-8651-c6fba9d86d91" "answer-542dff14-ba5a-5094-8199-ab519cc9d8ce" "answer-deeeee46-f112-5e27-a329-96e64bc24b65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49a263fb-b924-566b-a1a2-e05321e1d5e8" :answer/id #uuid "49a263fb-b924-566b-a1a2-e05321e1d5e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$  and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0dfb5d5-ea82-565b-84e6-679186a0f012" :answer/id #uuid "e0dfb5d5-ea82-565b-84e6-679186a0f012" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$  and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb250ee6-15f1-5344-8651-c6fba9d86d91" :answer/id #uuid "eb250ee6-15f1-5344-8651-c6fba9d86d91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$  and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-542dff14-ba5a-5094-8199-ab519cc9d8ce" :answer/id #uuid "542dff14-ba5a-5094-8199-ab519cc9d8ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-deeeee46-f112-5e27-a329-96e64bc24b65" :answer/id #uuid "deeeee46-f112-5e27-a329-96e64bc24b65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-71b4ed44-551f-59fd-a0cd-dc5bcd55b071" :question/id #uuid "71b4ed44-551f-59fd-a0cd-dc5bcd55b071" :question/math-academy-id "q-35271" :question/problem "If \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(B)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $B,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(B)=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2af22924-1cce-522c-aadc-abcfbbca5566"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2af22924-1cce-522c-aadc-abcfbbca5566" :answer-field/id #uuid "2af22924-1cce-522c-aadc-abcfbbca5566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f29b74c5-893c-5a44-8e76-6c39f0301bb2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be020027-00e4-5988-94b8-3d6ef8dffe52" "answer-d4a9245b-945c-5b2f-a3f2-23d524e7d6ca" "answer-f29b74c5-893c-5a44-8e76-6c39f0301bb2" "answer-080f7b68-1446-53cb-a768-ddfed5710a59" "answer-58ea38e8-5330-5713-ac69-29ba41df0ffb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be020027-00e4-5988-94b8-3d6ef8dffe52" :answer/id #uuid "be020027-00e4-5988-94b8-3d6ef8dffe52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4a9245b-945c-5b2f-a3f2-23d524e7d6ca" :answer/id #uuid "d4a9245b-945c-5b2f-a3f2-23d524e7d6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f29b74c5-893c-5a44-8e76-6c39f0301bb2" :answer/id #uuid "f29b74c5-893c-5a44-8e76-6c39f0301bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-080f7b68-1446-53cb-a768-ddfed5710a59" :answer/id #uuid "080f7b68-1446-53cb-a768-ddfed5710a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ea38e8-5330-5713-ac69-29ba41df0ffb" :answer/id #uuid "58ea38e8-5330-5713-ac69-29ba41df0ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120385 :question/problem "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]$, find $\\text{rank}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $A,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118424 :answer-field/correct 17592186118429 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}]
